All six features implemented in two files, verified with a 22-case TestClient run (all pass) plus `py_compile`.

**`app/auth.py:6-11`** — `require_api_key` now raises 401 on missing/invalid key and returns the username on success.

**`app/main.py`**:
- `list_tasks` (`app/main.py:16-32`) — optional `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` filters, combinable; `page` (default 1) and `page_size` (default 20), both validated `ge=1`, applied after filtering.
- `create_task` (`app/main.py:34-45`) — auth via `Depends(require_api_key)`, 404 when `project_id` doesn't exist, ID generated as `max(existing)+1`, returns the created task.
- `update_task` (`app/main.py:47-59`) — auth, partial updates via `model_dump(exclude_unset=True)`, 404 if not found.
- `delete_task` (`app/main.py:61-70`) — auth, returns the removed task, 404 if not found.

Notes on judgment calls:
- `GET /tasks` stays public — the spec required auth only on the write endpoints, so I didn't add it to reads.
- Create/update/delete return 200 with the task body, matching the existing `get_task` pattern (no `201`/`204`).
- The unused return value of `require_api_key` is intentional — the dependency's validation is the side effect that matters.
